    "title": "Brian Knox named new assistant chief of police for Shafter Police Department - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jacqueline Gutierrez ,\n8 hours ago\nBAKERSFIELD, Calif. (KGET) — Former McFarland Chief of Police Brian Knox has been appointed as the Shafter Police Department’s assistant chief of police.\nOfficials with the Shafter Police Department said Knox has an “extensive background,” with law enforcement, leadership and a commitment to integrity, professionalism and a vision that is necessary to guide the Shafter Police Department.\nKnox’s appointment as the assistant chief of police was effective Nov. 17.\nKnox’s career began back in 1992 as a detentions deputy for the Kern County Sheriff’s Office and went on to serve as sergeant, captain and then chief of police of the McFarland Police Department, which he was appointed to in 2023.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KGET 17 News.",
